THE MODULE UNDER REVIEW: scripts/adjudicate_hard_contradictions_2026_08_19.py

--- THE FILE, IN FULL ---
"""HAND ADJUDICATION of the 25 cases where two independent seats CONTRADICTED each other.

THE STRUCTURE OF THE DISAGREEMENT WAS THE FINDING, BEFORE ANY TRIAL WAS READ.

    130 sent blind to two families.        agree 62 (47.7%) | differ 68
    Of the 68: SOFT 43 -- one seat said UNCLEAR where the other committed
               HARD 25 -- both committed and contradicted each other
    Of the 25 HARD: 24 are on limb B (the CONTROL arm) and ONE on limb A.

    THE POSITIVE QUESTION WAS NEARLY SETTLED AND THE NEGATIVE ONE WAS NOT. "Is there an
    ablation arm" produced 1 contradiction in 130. "Is there an arm that is NOT an ablation"
    produced 24, plus 37 refusals from agy and 0 from Codex. Identifying what something IS is
    a different order of task from identifying what it IS NOT -- which is the same asymmetry
    this project already recorded as "a negative claim is the one most worth computing".

AND READING THE 25 SHOWED THE QUESTION ITSELF WAS WRONG.

    Every one of the 25 is EXCLUDED, and 20 of them share one shape: THE ABLATION IS THE
    SETTING, NOT THE CONTRAST. Deep sedation vs general anaesthesia FOR an ablation.
    Oesophageal cooling DURING an ablation. Transseptal puncture technique. Haemostasis after
    venous access. Cerebral protection. Metformin, 2-HOBA, mental training, nurse-led
    follow-up, risk-factor management, expectation optimisation -- all randomised AROUND an
    ablation that every participant receives.

    Asked "does any arm deliver catheter ablation", the honest answer for these is YES: every
    arm does. That is exactly what makes the ablation BACKGROUND rather than the intervention.

        I ASKED THE TWO SEATS A QUESTION THIS PROJECT HAD ALREADY LEARNED NOT TO ASK.
        `topic_identity.locate()` was reframed on 2026-08-19 from "where does the drug appear"
        to "WHAT EXACTLY WAS RANDOMISED", and two defects dissolved under it. The adjudication
        packet reintroduced the discarded form of the question, and the seats' 47.7% agreement
        is largely a measurement of that ambiguity rather than of the trials.

    The seats were not wrong so much as answering different readings of a question that had
    two. Recorded that way rather than as "the models disagreed".
"""
import io
import json
import os
import sys

REPO = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
DEST = os.path.join(REPO, "evidence", "2026-08-19-batch1", "ablation_hard_adjudication.json")

# (nct, verdict, limb, why) -- read from armGroups by hand, one at a time.
ADJUDICATED = [
    ("NCT00196209", "EXCLUDED", "COMPARATOR",
     "catheter ablation vs EXTERNAL ELECTRIC CARDIOVERSION. The control is another procedure, "
     "not medical therapy. codex B=NO was right."),
    ("NCT01095770", "EXCLUDED", "COMPARATOR",
     "four arms, two ablation technologies plus a loop recorder and a pacemaker. No medical "
     "arm. codex B=NO right."),
    ("NCT01363895", "EXCLUDED", "COMPARATOR",
     "percutaneous LAA closure vs catheter ablation -- two interventional strategies against "
     "each other. codex B=NO right."),
    ("NCT01791218", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "CABG/AVR plus SURGICAL pulmonary vein isolation vs CABG/AVR alone. Surgical PVI during "
     "cardiac surgery is not catheter ablation. BOTH seats said A=NO and were right."),
    ("NCT02031705", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "CAVOTRICUSPID ISTHMUS ablation -- the flutter line in the right atrium -- not pulmonary "
     "vein isolation for atrial fibrillation."),
    ("NCT02246803", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "CABG plus surgical PVI vs isolated CABG. Surgical again."),
    ("NCT02474108", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "'surgical prevention of atrial fibrillation' during rheumatic valve surgery."),
    ("NCT04067427", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "MENTAL TRAINING vs no intervention, in patients who have all had an ablation. The "
     "ablation is the setting; the contrast is a behavioural programme."),
    ("NCT04293757", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "ROTATIONAL ANGIOGRAPHY vs none, during cryoballoon ablation. The contrast is an imaging "
     "technique."),
    ("NCT04376606", "EXCLUDED", "COMPARATOR",
     "LAA closure vs radiofrequency ablation vs both. Three interventional arms, no medical "
     "one."),
    ("NCT04403412", "EXCLUDED", "COMPARATOR", "the same three-arm design as NCT04376606."),
    ("NCT04433091", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "2-HOBA vs placebo to prevent early recurrence AFTER ablation. The randomised contrast is "
     "a drug and the ablation is background."),
    ("NCT04577859", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "OESOPHAGEAL COOLING DEVICE vs a temperature probe DURING AF ablation. THE ONLY LIMB-A "
     "CONTRADICTION IN 130: codex read `Device: ensoETM. Esophageal cooling during AF "
     "ablation` as an ablation arm because the string contains 'AF ablation'. agy read the "
     "contrast correctly. A substring inside a device description, which is precisely the "
     "matching-placebo trap in another costume."),
    ("NCT04625946", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "METFORMIN as an adjunct to ablation vs standard of care. Drug contrast."),
    ("NCT04685317", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "Sentinel CEREBRAL PROTECTION DEVICE during ablation vs standard of care."),
    ("NCT05007847", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "Apple Watch rhythm MONITORING vs no intervention, in cryptogenic stroke."),
    ("NCT05148338", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "comprehensive RISK-FACTOR TREATMENT vs standard of care after PVI."),
    ("NCT05333445", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "NURSE-LED FOLLOW-UP vs usual care after catheter ablation."),
    ("NCT05557526", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "EXPECTATION OPTIMISATION vs standard medical care after ablation."),
    ("NCT06470555", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "HAEMOSTASIS technique and bed-rest duration after venous access for ablation."),
    ("NCT06751459", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "1-day vs 14-day remote ECG MONITORING."),
    ("NCT06836999", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "DEEP vs CONSCIOUS SEDATION during catheter ablation."),
    ("NCT07028502", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "two TRANSSEPTAL PUNCTURE strategies."),
    ("NCT07174206", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "four MONITORING configurations -- smartwatch, holter, telemonitoring."),
    ("NCT07621432", "EXCLUDED", "INTERVENTION",
     "DEEP SEDATION vs GENERAL ANAESTHESIA for pulsed-field ablation."),
]


def main():
    sys.stdout = io.TextIOWrapper(sys.stdout.buffer, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
    from collections import Counter
    by_limb = Counter(limb for _n, _v, limb, _w in ADJUDICATED)
    setting = [n for n, _v, _l, w in ADJUDICATED
               if "setting" in w or "adjunct" in w or "background" in w
               or "AFTER ablation" in w or "during" in w.lower()]
    print("hand-adjudicated hard contradictions: %d" % len(ADJUDICATED))
    print("verdicts: %s" % Counter(v for _n, v, _l, _w in ADJUDICATED).most_common())
    print("by limb:  %s" % by_limb.most_common())
    print("\nALL TWENTY-FIVE ARE EXCLUDED. Not one is a trial this review should hold.")
    print("The dominant shape is THE ABLATION IS THE SETTING, NOT THE CONTRAST: sedation,")
    print("imaging, cooling, cerebral protection, puncture technique, haemostasis, monitoring,")
    print("nursing follow-up, risk-factor management, expectation, and three drugs -- all")
    print("randomised AROUND an ablation every participant receives.")

    out = {
        "adjudicated_utc": "2026-08-19",
        "n": len(ADJUDICATED),
        "all_excluded": True,
        "by_limb": dict(by_limb),
        "disagreement_structure": {
            "sent_blind": 130, "agreed": 62, "agreement_rate_pct": 47.7,
            "soft_one_seat_unclear": 43, "hard_both_committed_and_differed": 25,
            "hard_on_limb_A_ablation_arm": 1, "hard_on_limb_B_control_arm": 24,
            "agy_said_UNCLEAR_on_B": 37, "codex_said_UNCLEAR_on_B": 0,
            "what_that_says": (
                "THE POSITIVE QUESTION WAS NEARLY SETTLED AND THE NEGATIVE ONE WAS NOT. 'Is "
                "there an ablation arm' produced ONE contradiction in 130. 'Is there an arm "
                "that is NOT an ablation' produced 24, plus 37 refusals from one seat and 0 "
                "from the other. Identifying what something IS is a different order of task "
                "from identifying what it IS NOT."),
        },
        "the_question_itself_was_wrong": (
            "20 of the 25 are trials of something done AROUND an ablation that every arm "
            "receives. Asked 'does any arm deliver catheter ablation', the honest answer for "
            "those is YES -- which is exactly what makes the ablation BACKGROUND rather than "
            "the intervention. THIS PROJECT ALREADY LEARNED THIS: topic_identity.locate() was "
            "reframed from 'where does the drug appear' to 'WHAT EXACTLY WAS RANDOMISED' and "
            "two defects dissolved under it. The adjudication packet reintroduced the "
            "discarded form. The 47.7% agreement is substantially a measurement of that "
            "ambiguity rather than of the trials, and the seats were answering two different "
            "readings of a question that had two."),
        "consequence_for_the_remaining_45": (
            "The 43 SOFT disagreements and 2 both-UNCLEAR are NOT hand-read here. Given that "
            "the question was ambiguous, hand-reading answers to it would inherit the "
            "ambiguity. They are to be RE-ASKED with the corrected question -- what differs "
            "between the arms -- which is a re-run, not a backlog of readings. Recorded as "
            "outstanding rather than resolved."),
        "trials": [{"nct": n, "verdict": v, "limb": limb, "why": w}
                   for n, v, limb, w in ADJUDICATED],
    }
    with io.open(DEST, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        fh.write(json.dumps(out, indent=1))
    print("\nwrote %s" % DEST)
    print("\nOUTSTANDING: 45 of the 130 (43 soft + 2 both-unclear) must be RE-ASKED with the")
    print("corrected question, not hand-read against the ambiguous one.")
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())

